#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:39
msgid ""
" <qt> <p><b>Print Job Billing and Accounting</b></p>  <p>Insert a meaningful "
"string here to associate the current print job with a certain account. This "
"string will appear in the CUPS \"page_log\" to help with the print "
"accounting in your organization. (Leave it empty if you do not need it.)</p> "
"<p> It is useful for people who print on behalf of different \"customers\", "
"like print service bureaux, letter shops, press and prepress companies, or "
"secretaries who serve different bosses, etc.</p> <br />  <hr />  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"corresponds to the CUPS command line job option parameter:</em>  <pre>    -o "
"job-billing=...         # example: \"Marketing_Department\" or \"Joe_Doe\"  "
"</pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> <p><b>Naplata i predračun printanog zadatka</b></p> <p>Ubaciti smislen "
"niz ovdje da biste povezali do sada isprintan zadataksa trenutnim nalogom. "
"Ovaj niz će se pojaviti u CUPS \"page_log\" za pomoć pri printanju "
"predračuna u vašoj organizaciji.(Ostavite prazno polje ako vam nije "
"potreban.))</p> <p>  Koristan je za ljude koji printaju  u ime različitih "
"korisnika,kao print usluga bureaux, trgovine pismima, štampa i "
"predštamparske kompanije ili sekretari koji rade kod nekoliko šefova, itd.</"
"p> <br /> <hr /> <p><em><b> Dodatni savjet za napredne korisnike:</b> Ovaj "
"KDEPrint GUI element odgovara CUPS komandi opcije parametra:</em> <pre> -o "
"job-billing=... # example: \"Marketing_Department\" or \"Joe_Doe\" </pre> </"
"p> </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:59
msgid ""
" <qt> <p><b>Scheduled Printing</b></p>  <p>Scheduled printing lets you "
"control the time of the actual printout, while you can still send away your "
"job <b>now</b> and have it out of your way.</p> <p> Especially useful is the "
"\"Never (hold indefinitely)\" option. It allows you to park your job until a "
"time when you (or a printer administrator) decides to manually release it.</"
"p> <p> This is often required in enterprise environments, where you normally "
"are not allowed to directly and immediately access the huge production "
"printers in your <em>Central Repro Department</em>. However it is okay to "
"send jobs to the queue which is under the control of the operators (who, "
"after all, need to make sure that the 10,000 sheets of pink paper which is "
"required by the Marketing Department for a particular job are available and "
"loaded into the paper trays.)</p> <br />  <hr />  <p><em><b>Additional hint "
"for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element corresponds to the CUPS "
"command line job option parameter:</em>  <pre>    -o job-hold-until=...      "
"# example: \"indefinite\" or \"no-hold\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> <p><b> Planirano/zakazano printanje </b></p> <p> Planirano printanje "
"vam omogućava da kontrolirate vrijeme printanja,dok još možete odgoditi svoj "
"zadatak <b>now</b> i zadržati ga. Posebno korisna je ' Nikad(zadrži "
"neograničeno' opcija. Dozvoljava Vam da zadržite svoj zadatak dok vi(ili "
"printer administrator) ne odlučite ručno da ga pustite. </p> <p> Ovo je "
"često potrebno u poduzetnim okruženjima,gdje vam  obično nije odobreno da "
"odmah direktno pristupite velikim produkcijama printera u vašim <em>Central "
"Repro Department</em>. U svakom slučaju u redu je da pošaljete svoj zadatak "
"u red koji je pod kontrolom operatora(koji,ipak,moraju da budu sigurni da "
"10,000 stranica roze papira koji je potrban za Odsijek Marketinga za "
"određeni posao je dostupan i učitan na platoe papira.))</p> <br /> <hr /> "
"<p><em><b> Dodatni savjet za napredne korisnike: </b>Ovaj KDEPrint GUI "
"element odgovara CUPS komandi opcije parametra:</em> <pre> -o job-hold-"
"until=... # example: \"indefinite\" or \"no-hold\" </pre> </p> </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:86
msgid ""
" <qt> <p><b>Page Labels</b></p>  <p>Page Labels are printed by CUPS at the "
"top and bottom of each page. They appear on the pages surrounded by a little "
"frame box.</p> <p>They contain any string you type into the line edit field."
"</p> <br />  <hr />  <p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This "
"KDEPrint GUI element corresponds to the CUPS command line job option "
"parameter:</em>  <pre>    -o page-label=\"...\"      # example: \"Company "
"Confidential\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> <p><b>Oznake stranica</b></p> <p>Oznake stranica su printane CUPSom na "
"početku i kraju svake stranice.One se pojavljuju na stranicama okruženim "
"malim okvirom. </p> <p> One sadrže bilo koji niz koji ukucate u liniju za "
"uređivanje polja.</p> <br /> <hr /> <p><em><b> Dodatni savjet za napredne "
"korisnike: </b>Ovaj KDEPrint GUI element odgovara CUPS komandi opcije "
"parametra:</em> <pre> -o page-label=\"...\" # example: \"Company Confidential"
"\" </pre> </p> </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:101
msgid ""
" <qt> <p><b>Job Priority</b></p>  <p>Usually CUPS prints all jobs per queue "
"according to the \"FIFO\" principle: <em>First In, First Out</em>.</p> <p> "
"The job priority option allows you to re-order the queue according to your "
"needs.</p> <p> It works in both directions: you can increase as well as "
"decrease priorities. (Usually you can only control your <b>own</b> jobs.)</"
"p> <p> Since the default job priority is \"50\", any job sent with, for "
"example, \"49\" will be printed only after all those others have finished. "
"Conversely, a \"51\" or higher priority job will go right to the top of a "
"populated queue (if no other, higher prioritized one is present.)</p> <br /"
">  <hr />  <p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI "
"element corresponds to the CUPS command line job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o job-priority=...   # example: \"10\" or \"66\" or \"99\"  </pre> "
"</p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> <p><b> Prioritet zadatka </b></p> <p> Obično CUPS printa sve zadatke "
"po redu prema ''FIFO'' principu : <em>First In, First Out</em>.</p> <p> "
"Opcija za prioritet zadatka vam omogućuje da poredate red prema vašim "
"potrebama.</p> <p> On djeluje u oba smijera:možete povećati kao i smanjiti "
"prioritet.(Obično možete kontrolirati svoje <b>own</b> zadatke.)</p> <p> "
"Kako je zadani prioritet zadatka ''50'',svaki zadatak poslan sa na "
"primer,''49'' bit će printan samo nakon što su ostali isprintani.Suprotno "
"tome,''51'' ili više prioritetni zadaci će biti na samom vrhu reda(ako nema "
"drugog,više prioritetan zadatak je prisutan).</p> <br /> <hr /> <p><em><b> "
"Dodatni savjet za napredne korisnike:</b> Ovaj KDEPrint GUI element odgovara "
"CUPS komandi opcije parametra:</em> <pre> -o job-priority=... # primjer: "
"\"10\" ili \"66\" ili \"99\" </pre> </p> </qt>"

